# YouTube Core and Live Streaming

Lux provides YouTube Data API v3 helpers for agents that need to manage channels, video upload sessions, live broadcasts, live streams, and live chat.

## Authentication

Configure OAuth credentials and an access token:

```elixir
config :lux, :api_keys,
  youtube_client_id: System.fetch_env!("YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID"),
  youtube_client_secret: System.fetch_env!("YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET"),
  youtube_access_token: System.fetch_env!("YOUTUBE_ACCESS_TOKEN")
```

Build a consent URL when onboarding a channel:

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.YouTube.oauth_authorization_url(%{
  redirect_uri: "http://localhost:4000/oauth/youtube",
  state: "csrf-token"
})
```

The default scopes cover channel management, video uploads, live streaming, and live chat moderation.

## Channel Metadata

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.Channels.ListChannels

{:ok, channels} =
  ListChannels.focus(%{
    mine: true,
    max_results: 5
  })
```

## Resumable Upload Setup

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Videos.StartResumableUpload

{:ok, %{upload_url: upload_url}} =
  StartResumableUpload.handler(
    %{
      title: "Agent update",
      description: "Generated by a Lux workflow",
      privacy_status: "private",
      content_type: "video/mp4",
      content_length: 12_000_000
    },
    %{name: "Publisher"}
  )
```

The returned `upload_url` is the session URL used by the caller to upload video bytes.

## Live Broadcast Workflow

Create a broadcast:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Live.CreateBroadcast

{:ok, broadcast} =
  CreateBroadcast.handler(
    %{
      title: "Launch stream",
      scheduled_start_time: "2026-05-18T00:00:00Z",
      privacy_status: "unlisted"
    },
    %{name: "Producer"}
  )
```

Create a stream target:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Live.CreateStream

{:ok, stream} =
  CreateStream.handler(
    %{
      title: "Primary ingest",
      resolution: "1080p",
      frame_rate: "60fps"
    },
    %{name: "Producer"}
  )
```

Bind and transition:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Live.BindBroadcast
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Live.TransitionBroadcast

{:ok, _bound} =
  BindBroadcast.handler(
    %{broadcast_id: broadcast.id, stream_id: stream.id},
    %{name: "Producer"}
  )

{:ok, _testing} =
  TransitionBroadcast.handler(
    %{broadcast_id: broadcast.id, broadcast_status: "testing"},
    %{name: "Producer"}
  )
```

## Health and Chat

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.Live.StreamHealth
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.Live.ListChatMessages
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Live.SendChatMessage

{:ok, streams} = StreamHealth.focus(%{id: stream.id})

{:ok, chat} =
  ListChatMessages.focus(%{
    live_chat_id: broadcast.live_chat_id,
    max_results: 100
  })

{:ok, _sent} =
  SendChatMessage.handler(
    %{live_chat_id: broadcast.live_chat_id, message: "Welcome to the stream"},
    %{name: "Moderator"}
  )
```

`Lux.Integrations.YouTube.LiveStream.transition_plan/2` can be used to derive safe transitions such as `ready -> testing -> live`.
